      "effectContract": {
        "id": "ntilde-kitty-unicode-placeholders-persistent-effect-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "statement": "In a persistent tab (persistent image policy 5), Kitty Unicode placeholders behave as the Kitty protocol specifies, read by paired offscreen captures of one row of two cells: a transmitted 16x16 image (left half red, right half blue) with a virtual placement (a=p,U=1) of a 2 x 1 grid draws nothing by itself; cells printing U+10EEEE whose foreground colour names the image, whose underline colour names the placement and whose row and column diacritics name tiles (0,0) and (0,1) show the red half and then the blue half, each tile an undistorted band of its own color; erasing the cells removes the image; the diacritics and not the screen position choose the tile (swapped columns swap the colors, and a lone cell naming column 0 shows the red half wherever it is printed); a bare placeholder after a cell with marks (row 0, column 0) continues in row 0 at the next column (inheritance of a nonzero row is not measured: the grid has one row); cells naming an image that was never transmitted, a placement that does not exist, or a tile outside the grid paint nothing while the valid cells (the positive control) do, and deleting the image's placements (a=d,d=i) makes those same cells paint nothing again. Every command that expects a Kitty reply returned OK (the virtual placement's reply echoes its placement id), and each clear passed its fence and left its target blank (a=d success is silent).",
        "primary": "https://sw.kovidgoyal.net/kitty/graphics-protocol/#unicode-placeholders",
        "carrierCases": [
          "kitty.placeholders.tiles",
          "kitty.placeholders.cell-mapping",
          "kitty.placeholders.unbound"
        ],
